warrior | Tell Lena you have news you have been putting off all night.
warrior | Tell her you leave at dawn to guard a caravan to the far coast, and you will be gone for months.
warrior | Ask her, as a question to her, whether she will think of you while you are gone.
warrior | Tell her you wish you had met her before you took the job.
warrior | Ask her, as a question to her, whether you can write to her from the road.
warrior | Ask her, as a question to her, whether she will still be here when you come back.
warrior | Tell her, simply, that you are falling for her.
warrior | Say goodbye; ask her, as a question to her, for something to remember her by.
